## fix(reasoning): aggregate rules never materialized their result class

Context: an Aggregate rule with a Result entity (e.g. BlendWine = Wine with
COUNT(containsGrape) > 1 -> typed BlendWine) computed and flagged matches but
never materialized the `rdf:type <result_class>` triples — the Inference report
always showed "No new findings" for the Aggregate phase. Root cause:
`AggregateRuleEngine._execute_one` only appended its inferred triple when the
engine was called with `materialize=True`, but the UI Inference Run passes
`materialize=False` and defers the write to the separate Materialise step (which
persists the task's stored `inferred_triples`). SWRL and Decision engines append
their inferred triples unconditionally and only use `materialize` for an extra
direct store write — which is why greatWine / tastingTier materialized but
aggregate output never reached the materialise step.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/reasoning/rules/AggregateRuleEngine.py — emit the
   `rdf:type <result_class_uri>` inferred triple whenever the rule declares a
   result class, regardless of the `materialize` flag (consistent with
   SWRL/Decision: the engine always RETURNS its triples; the caller decides
   whether to persist). Rules without a result class still only report
   violations.
2. tests/units/ontology/test_business_rules.py — a matching row emits the
   classification triple with `materialize=False`; a rule without a result
   class reports only a violation.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/reasoning/rules/AggregateRuleEngine.py
- tests/units/ontology/test_business_rules.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" tests/units/dtwin tests/units/ontology/test_business_rules.py` -> 743 passed. Full suite -> pending (see PR).
